♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC INTENSIFIES) ♪

00:02:28.231 --> 00:02:31.734
ROSE: Remotes,
bobby pins, socks,

00:02:32.193 --> 00:02:35.613
a favorite V-neck...
All the replaceable things

00:02:35.697 --> 00:02:38.157
that we tend to fret over
when they are lost

00:02:38.241 --> 00:02:39.617
or simply misplaced.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.745
But when it comes
to missing black girls,

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:48.167
it's a topic often overlooked.
No one checks the crevices

00:02:48.251 --> 00:02:51.713
of the couch, behind the dryer,
the junk drawer.

00:02:52.046 --> 00:02:54.173
It seems as though
these missing black girls

00:02:54.257 --> 00:02:56.634
are just... forgotten.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:58.761
And it's nothing new.

00:02:59.095 --> 00:03:01.431
This has been an issue
for years.

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:04.684
And think about it...
We still haven't found

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:07.270
the original dark-skinned Claire
from My Wife and Kids.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:10.106
(SIGHS) But that's
another podcast.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:15.028
This podcast is about
26-year-old LaToya Thompson.

00:03:15.111 --> 00:03:17.030
-(DOOR CREAKS OPEN)
-PETEY: Hey, Rose...

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.782
-You seen my Texas toast?
-(ROSE GROANS)

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.951
-(DOOR CLOSES)
-(POTS AND PANS CLANG)

00:03:23.912 --> 00:03:25.330
ROSE:
For the last nine years,

00:03:25.413 --> 00:03:27.165
I've proudly served
as the certified

00:03:27.248 --> 00:03:29.918
theft specialist
and chief investigative officer

00:03:30.126 --> 00:03:33.296
for Burlington Coat Factory
back in Atlanta, Georgia.

00:03:34.422 --> 00:03:37.133
Although it's just called
Burlington now.

00:03:38.134 --> 00:03:41.638
Anyway... My job
has always required me

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:44.390
to have a very keen sense
of detail.

00:03:44.807 --> 00:03:49.103
After years of monitoring
both entrance and exit doors,

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.565
screening hardcore criminals,
reviewing top-secret

00:03:52.649 --> 00:03:56.319
security footage, and binging
 Law and Order repeats...

00:03:57.528 --> 00:03:58.780
There's not much

00:03:58.988 --> 00:04:00.323
that can get past me.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:06.037
I pay attention to things.
I notice things.

00:04:06.287 --> 00:04:07.956
("LAW AND ORDER"
TONE PLAYS)

00:04:08.164 --> 00:04:11.417
See at Burlington,
we have an array of customers.

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:14.253
But we also have
our committed regulars,

00:04:14.504 --> 00:04:16.881
who frequent the store
on a weekly basis.

00:04:17.507 --> 00:04:20.551
One of those people
was Glenda Thompson.

00:04:21.052 --> 00:04:23.346
Glenda typically came in
once a week

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:27.100
to browse linens
and stock up on scented candles.

00:04:27.183 --> 00:04:28.935
Oftentimes,
she'd be accompanied

00:04:29.018 --> 00:04:31.688
by her 26-year-old
daughter, LaToya.

00:04:32.188 --> 00:04:36.067
They were both so friendly.
And always smiling,

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:38.027
and made sure to greet me.

00:04:38.861 --> 00:04:41.030
We even spoke from time
to time.

00:04:41.572 --> 00:04:43.908
I remember the day Glenda
came in alone.

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:47.537
And she told me that LaToya
had moved to Los Angeles

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.581
to be a star.
Which came as no surprise

00:04:50.665 --> 00:04:53.751
to me because I'd often
see LaToya twerking

00:04:53.835 --> 00:04:54.961
for the store cameras.

00:04:55.044 --> 00:04:56.796
(TAPE REEL SPINS CHAOTICALLY)

00:04:56.879 --> 00:04:59.841
(OVERLAPPING CHATTER, CHEERING)

00:05:03.553 --> 00:05:06.556
But after a few weeks,
I noticed something

00:05:06.764 --> 00:05:10.727
had changed with Glenda.
She stopped greeting me.

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:13.563
Her linen selection got lazy.

00:05:14.564 --> 00:05:17.316
Her smile had completely faded.

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:21.362
It looked as though something
was weighing on her.

00:05:22.071 --> 00:05:23.698
Something heavy.

00:05:24.407 --> 00:05:27.076
So I approached her
with a few questions.

00:05:29.078 --> 00:05:30.872
(TAPE DECK CLICKING)

00:05:30.955 --> 00:05:34.000
INTERCOM: Attention shoppers,
 Burlington will be closing

00:05:34.083 --> 00:05:35.460
in 15 minutes.

00:05:36.085 --> 00:05:37.837
GLENDA: All I really know
 is that she moved in

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.840
with a girl named Tasha.
Said she signed up

00:05:40.923 --> 00:05:42.884
for some overpriced
acting class,

00:05:42.967 --> 00:05:44.385
taught by a renowned actor.

00:05:44.635 --> 00:05:46.763
But I couldn't even find him
on Google.

00:05:47.638 --> 00:05:49.807
She started fooling
with some guy named Rufus,

00:05:50.099 --> 00:05:51.726
and said he was on his way
to being one

00:05:51.809 --> 00:05:53.770
of those influencers.

00:05:54.312 --> 00:05:56.439
She mentioned something
about his teeth.

00:05:56.522 --> 00:06:01.319
Um, they're loose, or dead,
maybe both.

00:06:02.445 --> 00:06:04.447
I knew we should have never
let her leave Atlanta.

00:06:07.283 --> 00:06:08.701
ROSE: Glenda went on
to tell me

00:06:08.785 --> 00:06:11.037
she hadn't heard from LaToya
in quite some time.

00:06:11.329 --> 00:06:13.539
She was officially announced
as missing,

00:06:13.623 --> 00:06:15.875
and had been since July 23rd.

00:06:16.292 --> 00:06:18.878
The last place she'd been
seen was at a Red Lobster

00:06:18.961 --> 00:06:21.672
in Inglewood, California.
That's when...

00:06:21.756 --> 00:06:24.675
PETEY: I found the Texas toast.
Rose, you want some Texas--

00:06:24.759 --> 00:06:27.011
ROSE: No! Petey! Damn,
can't you see I'm on--

00:06:27.345 --> 00:06:31.682
I'm recording.
(SIGHS)

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:34.143
Sorry.
Like I was saying,

00:06:34.519 --> 00:06:36.479
that's when I knew I had
to help.

00:06:36.813 --> 00:06:39.398
Glenda explained to me
that LaToya was missing,

00:06:39.482 --> 00:06:43.027
and to no surprise,
no one seemed to care.

00:06:43.528 --> 00:06:47.406
I felt with all my experience
in resolving shoplifting cases,

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.618
catching petty criminals,
and assessing missing items,

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:53.579
it was a chance for me
to step up.

00:06:54.288 --> 00:06:57.250
It was time for me
to do something more important

00:06:57.333 --> 00:07:01.504
than loss prevention:
lost girls prevention.

00:07:01.963 --> 00:07:05.007
But just the black ones.
The white ones are fine.

00:07:06.175 --> 00:07:09.887
That's when I decided
to pursue my own investigation,

00:07:10.138 --> 00:07:13.516
make my way to Los Angeles
and start this podcast.

00:07:14.851 --> 00:07:17.854
I've also been told
that I have a good radio voice.

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:19.605
I've occasionally been asked
to make

00:07:19.689 --> 00:07:22.191
the intercom announcements
in the department store.

00:07:22.441 --> 00:07:23.484
(INTERCOM FEEDBACK)

00:07:24.318 --> 00:07:26.279
(OVER INTERCOM) Leanne,
 you're needed at the register.

00:07:26.362 --> 00:07:28.364
Leanne, needed at the register.

00:07:32.034 --> 00:07:36.038
(CLOCK TICKING)

00:07:41.836 --> 00:07:45.923
(SIPPING DRINK, CLEARS THROAT)

00:07:48.718 --> 00:07:51.888
Biscuits...
Cheddar Bay Biscuits.

00:07:52.221 --> 00:07:54.849
A convenient and delicious
luxury for many.

00:07:55.099 --> 00:07:57.894
But for LaToya,
it might have been

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:00.605
the bite between life and death.

00:08:01.397 --> 00:08:04.775
Who's responsible?
Did anyone see this coming?

00:08:04.859 --> 00:08:06.485
Could anyone have stopped it?

00:08:06.903 --> 00:08:09.238
Is LaToya just missing?

00:08:09.906 --> 00:08:14.952
-Or was she... murdered?
-(SCREAMING)

00:08:15.036 --> 00:08:16.787
I was determined to find out.

00:08:17.163 --> 00:08:19.457
When I arrived in LA,
I decided

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:22.752
to start my investigation
Jehovah-Witness style,

00:08:23.085 --> 00:08:25.630
going door-to-door
in LaToya's neighborhood.

00:08:27.965 --> 00:08:30.092
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.095
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

00:08:34.805 --> 00:08:38.434
-(DOOR CREAKS OPEN)
 -Have you seen this girl?

00:08:38.601 --> 00:08:40.311
MAN: Nah, have you?

00:08:41.103 --> 00:08:43.189
ROSE: No, that's
 why I was ask--

00:08:43.272 --> 00:08:45.066
-(DOOR SHUTS)
 -Okay.

00:08:46.567 --> 00:08:50.571
-(DOGS BARKING)
-(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

00:08:52.615 --> 00:08:55.576
-(DOOR CREAKS OPEN)
-ROSE: Hi, have you seen--

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.495
WOMAN: I done told
 y'all motherfuckers,

00:08:57.578 --> 00:08:58.955
I ain't selling my house.

00:09:04.043 --> 00:09:09.715
-(NEIGHBORS CHATTERING)
-(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

00:09:09.799 --> 00:09:11.217
(DOOR CREAKS OPEN)

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:13.261
♪ (LOUD HIP-HOP MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:09:13.344 --> 00:09:17.848
ROSE: Uh, hi!
 Does this girl look familiar

00:09:17.932 --> 00:09:20.601
-to you?
-MAN: Oh, shit.

00:09:20.685 --> 00:09:22.478
Ain't that the original
little sister

00:09:22.562 --> 00:09:25.439
from My Wife and Kids?
 The dark-skinned one?

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:27.483
I'm glad she good.

00:09:28.025 --> 00:09:29.318
♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:09:29.527 --> 00:09:31.529
ROSE: No.
No that was not

00:09:31.612 --> 00:09:34.240
the original sister
from My Wife and Kids,

00:09:34.615 --> 00:09:39.078
it was LaToya.
After spending hours

00:09:39.161 --> 00:09:41.289
checking all the
low-income apartments

00:09:41.372 --> 00:09:43.916
in the Inglewood area,
I was finally able

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.960
to track down
where LaToya lived.

00:09:46.836 --> 00:09:50.381
For a small exchange fee,
which I won't elaborate on,

00:09:50.673 --> 00:09:53.009
the landlord gave me
both LaToya

00:09:53.092 --> 00:09:55.928
and her roommate Tasha's
contact info.

00:09:56.512 --> 00:10:00.599
Of course, I called LaToya
to no avail.

00:10:01.058 --> 00:10:03.519
-(DIAL TONE BEEPING)
-SPOKESPERSON: We're sorry,

00:10:03.853 --> 00:10:05.604
the customer you are trying
to reach

00:10:05.688 --> 00:10:09.734
is currently unavailable.
Please hang up and try again.

00:10:10.359 --> 00:10:12.069
ROSE: I then dialed
Tasha,

00:10:12.153 --> 00:10:13.738
hoping to get an answer.

00:10:13.821 --> 00:10:15.156
TASHA: (OVER VOICEMAIL)
 You've reached Tasha!

00:10:15.239 --> 00:10:17.783
I ain't here, so you know
what to do, leave it.

00:10:17.867 --> 00:10:20.119
-(VOICEMAIL BEEPING)
-ROSE: Hi, Tasha,

00:10:20.202 --> 00:10:24.290
this is Rose Cranberry.
I'm calling about your roommate,

00:10:24.373 --> 00:10:26.959
LaToya Thompson.
Please call me back

00:10:27.043 --> 00:10:28.794
as soon as you can,
as I'm trying to gather

00:10:28.878 --> 00:10:30.755
some information
on her acting coach,

00:10:30.963 --> 00:10:32.965
or the friend
with the dead teeth.

00:10:33.382 --> 00:10:35.676
Hope to hear from you soon,
thanks.

00:10:36.552 --> 00:10:38.846
Much like the current state
of my hair,

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:44.060
I had hit another dead end.
So far I was getting nowhere.

00:10:45.061 --> 00:10:49.065
(CLOCK TICKING)

00:10:52.777 --> 00:10:54.487
(TAPE REEL SPINNING)

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:55.696
TRAVIS: I knew something
 was up

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.156
when she came in
with the white boy.

00:10:57.239 --> 00:10:59.658
STACY: Mm-hmm.
 Her "acting coach."

00:10:59.742 --> 00:11:02.328
They came for the
cheddar biscuits after class.

00:11:02.411 --> 00:11:03.579
(TAPE REEL STOPS SPINNING)

00:11:04.705 --> 00:11:05.998
ROSE: The voices
you just heard

00:11:06.082 --> 00:11:10.586
are that of two Red Lobster
employees, Travis and Stacy,

00:11:11.087 --> 00:11:13.089
who claim to have seen
LaToya last.

00:11:13.673 --> 00:11:15.758
I was able to sit down
with them both.

00:11:17.635 --> 00:11:18.969
TRAVIS: It was weird 'cause,
 you know,

00:11:19.178 --> 00:11:21.639
white people don't ever go
to the Inglewood Red Lobster.

00:11:21.722 --> 00:11:23.432
They always complain
the music's too loud.

00:11:23.516 --> 00:11:25.059
STACY: Yeah.
 Unless they tourists,

00:11:25.142 --> 00:11:26.977
and trying to experience
the hood.

00:11:27.436 --> 00:11:29.063
They usually go
to the one in Torrance.

00:11:29.355 --> 00:11:32.108
TRAVIS: Plus,
 we always out of salmon.

00:11:32.608 --> 00:11:33.567
They hate that.

00:11:34.068 --> 00:11:36.904
ROSE: I see. So tell me
 what you saw that day.

00:11:36.987 --> 00:11:38.030
♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:11:38.114 --> 00:11:39.323
STACY: Well...
 They was just sitting

00:11:39.407 --> 00:11:40.616
at the bar like they always do.

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:42.785
ROSE: So this was
 a regular thing?

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:45.287
STACY: Yep.
 They came in like once a week.

00:11:45.663 --> 00:11:47.665
But this time he was
looking suspicious.

00:11:47.957 --> 00:11:49.417
ROSE: And why is that?

00:11:49.708 --> 00:11:50.751
STACY: He was wearing a hoodie.

00:11:51.001 --> 00:11:52.837
TRAVIS: And he was drinking
 a Sprite with no ice.

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:54.630
That's serial killer shit.

00:11:55.339 --> 00:11:56.298
ROSE: I see.

00:11:56.465 --> 00:11:59.343
I was told LaToya had
a boyfriend.

00:11:59.802 --> 00:12:01.387
Do you think it's safe
to say

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:03.556
that she was having an affair
with this guy?

00:12:04.265 --> 00:12:05.975
TRAVIS:
 Man, I ain't no damn snitch.

00:12:06.767 --> 00:12:08.144
But I definitely think
he hit it.

00:12:08.477 --> 00:12:11.730
Ain't nobody just gone buy you
biscuits without some booty.

00:12:12.273 --> 00:12:13.983
And she always looked
hella happy.

00:12:14.275 --> 00:12:16.569
WOMAN: Yeah, but this time,
 he rushed out all quick.

00:12:16.944 --> 00:12:18.821
I think he left right when
the biscuits came.

00:12:19.071 --> 00:12:20.448
So, she was just sitting there
alone

00:12:20.531 --> 00:12:23.242
with a basket full of biscuits,
looking all inspired and shit.

00:12:23.742 --> 00:12:25.035
ROSE:
 And how long would you say

00:12:25.119 --> 00:12:27.121
LaToya sat there
before she left?

00:12:27.746 --> 00:12:30.166
WOMAN: I don't know.
 Maybe like 20 minutes.

00:12:30.374 --> 00:12:32.334
She was gone when I came back
from my break.

00:12:32.835 --> 00:12:34.336
